From 1e0dada6a9ee31973ec721e29aeb045bd7ab882a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:35:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] drm/apple: Fix a fixed 120 Hz ProMotion panel presenting
 at 60 Hz

A ProMotion panel whose 120 Hz timing comes without an adaptive-sync
range (both range fields zero, as the T6050 panel reports it, which
only desktop 26.x firmware turns into a 24-120 Hz range) parses as a
fixed timing: vrr is false, while needs_timestamps is still set for the
120 Hz rate. The desktop mode set already sends timestamps for such a
timing, but the mode set of every other firmware (12.3, 13.5, 27.x)
still keys them off vrr, so its swaps go out without presentation
timestamps and the firmware completes at most one per 16.7 ms: the panel
shows 60 frames a second at 120 Hz.

Key the swap timestamps off needs_timestamps there too, as the comment
above the line already says. Firmware 27 takes the same timestamps as
desktop 26.x: a swap stamped with ARM counter values is accepted and
never completed (the T6050 panel's first swap after the mode set timed
out that way and the processor was declared crashed), so send it the
desktop presentation deadline instead.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
index 824924238fa4..5dc4a606a6b1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
@@ -3814,8 +3814,12 @@ int DCP_FW_NAME(iomfb_modeset)(struct apple_dcp *dcp,
 	};
 	dcp->output_pq = dcp->pq_requested && mode->pq.score >= 0;
 
-	/* Built-in ProMotion panels require timestamps even in fixed-120 mode. */
-	dcp->use_timestamps = mode->vrr && dcp->main_display;
+	/*
+	 * Built-in ProMotion panels require timestamps even in fixed-120 mode:
+	 * a 120 Hz panel timing without an adaptive-sync range (vrr false)
+	 * still needs them, or the firmware completes one swap per 16.7 ms.
+	 */
+	dcp->use_timestamps = mode->needs_timestamps && dcp->main_display;
 
 	cookie = kzalloc(sizeof(*cookie), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!cookie) {
@@ -4090,6 +4094,15 @@ void DCP_FW_NAME(iomfb_flush)(struct apple_dcp *dcp, struct drm_crtc *crtc, stru
 		 */
 		if (!submit_timestamp)
 			submit_timestamp = timestamp;
+#if (DCP_FW_H17(DCP_FW_VER) && DCP_FW_VER >= DCP_FW_VERSION(27, 0, 0))
+		/*
+		 * Firmware 27 never completes a swap stamped with counter
+		 * values, as desktop 26.x: send its presentation deadline
+		 * long past, which asks for the next refresh.
+		 */
+		timestamp = dcp_desktop_present_deadline(true, true);
+		submit_timestamp = timestamp;
+#endif
 
 		/* Firmware 12.x/13.x requires timestamp types 1, 2, and 7. */
 		req->swap.timestamp[0] = timestamp;
-- 
